# Screen Transition Diagram: NBSP — NBC Blood Storage and Distribution Department

## 1. NBC Blood Storage and Distribution Department

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  entry(["Entry: opens NBSP URL"])
  entryA(["Entry: in-system alert notification"])
  S00_01["S-F00-01<br>Sign in"]
  S01_03["S-F01-03<br>Request Queue"]
  S01_04["S-F01-04<br>Review & Dispatch Request"]
  S02_02["S-F02-02<br>Inventory Dashboard"]
  S02_03["S-F02-03<br>Near-Expiry Units"]
  S02_04["S-F02-04<br>Alerts"]

  entry --> S00_01
  S00_01 -->|"[invalid credentials]"| S00_01
  S00_01 -->|"[signed in as Dept user]"| S01_03

  S01_03 -->|"selects a pending request"| S01_04
  S01_04 -->|"confirms in dialog [order dispatched]"| S01_03
  S01_04 -->|"[shortage, units no longer available or stock service unavailable]"| S01_04
  S01_04 -->|"back"| S01_03

  S01_03 -->|"nav: Inventory"| S02_02
  S02_02 -->|"nav: Requests"| S01_03
  S02_02 -->|"nav: Near-expiry"| S02_03
  S02_03 -->|"nav: Requests"| S01_03
  S02_03 -->|"nav: Inventory"| S02_02

  entryA --> S02_04
  S01_03 -->|"opens bell or nav: Alerts"| S02_04
  S02_04 -->|"opens stock of the blood type"| S02_02
  S02_04 -->|"nav: Requests"| S01_03

  S01_03 -->|"signs out"| S00_01
```

Conventions:

- Node ID: the Screen ID with `-` replaced by `_`; the label shows the real Screen ID.
- A modal is not a node: "confirms in dialog" is on the arrow.
- **Main navigation** is on every screen after sign-in: Requests · Inventory · Near-expiry · Alerts (bell) · Sign out. The diagram draws the arrows that matter; the full set is in the table.
- AD-UC-08 v0.4: the only successful outcome is Dispatched (back to the queue). Stock shortage, units no longer available and an unavailable stock service are states of S-F01-04: the staff stays on the screen, the request stays Pending. There is no "not approved" arrow.
- UC-17 (synchronisation) has no screen. Its effect is the timestamp on S-F02-02 and new alerts on S-F02-04.

| From \ To | S-F01-03 Requests | S-F02-02 Inventory | S-F02-03 Near-expiry | S-F02-04 Alerts | S-F00-01 Sign in |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| S-F01-03 | stays | nav | nav | nav / bell | sign out |
| S-F01-04 | back / dispatched | nav | nav | nav / bell | sign out |
| S-F02-02 | nav | stays | nav | nav / bell | sign out |
| S-F02-03 | nav | nav | stays | nav / bell | sign out |
| S-F02-04 | nav | link / nav | nav | stays | sign out |

The Operations (Forecast) side (NBC Forecasting Analyst, NBC Operations) uses the same sign-in screen and lands on its own start screen according to role and department (FR-04-02). NBC Operations also uses S-F02-02 and S-F02-04; its transition diagram belongs to the other owner.

